WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
Feynman learning technique is effective
full learning something new

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:06.990
deepen your understanding of what you
already know

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:09.780
or helping you study for an exam

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:16.320
the first step is to pick a topic
you want to understand and start studying it.

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:21.080
once you know what it is
about take a piece of paper and write about it

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:24.080
as if you're teaching the idea to someone else

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:30.400
ideally write and speak at the same time
just as a teacher does it at the blackboard

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:35.980
this makes you realize which part you
understand and where you still have gaps

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:41.180
whenever you get stuck go back to study
and repeat that process until you have

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:44.700
explained the whole topic from start to
end

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:51.780
when you're done repeat the process from the beginning
but this time simplify your language or

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:54.270
use a graphic analogy to make a point

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:57.840
if your explanation ends up wordy or
confusing

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.620
you probably have not understood it well
enough so you should start again

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:09.060
thinking about an idea by explaining it
makes this learning method very effective

00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:14.189
once you can explain an idea in simple
language you have deeply understood it

00:01:14.189 --> 00:01:17.189
and will remember it for a long time

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:22.420
Richard Feynman was a leading
theoretical physicist who received a

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:27.890
Nobel Prize for his work in quantum
electrodynamics

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:32.630
he was notorious for asking his fellow mathematicians to explain concepts in simple language

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:34.580
to test their understanding

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:38.400
thanks for watching

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:41.080
also check out others Sprouts learning
techniques

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:45.340
as they can complement the methods explained in this video

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:50.560
please use the comments below to give us feedback or tell us which of the
techniques is your favorite

